13:58.310 --> 14:02.010
<i>the marathon, where placement 
would make a huge difference.</i>

14:02.670 --> 14:05.130
Yukimura's Group
 First Runner: Sumida

14:05.920 --> 14:07.870
Ichi Springs
 Oshin River

14:10.390 --> 14:12.120
Second Runner: Moriyama

14:14.620 --> 14:18.130
Third Runner: Totsuka

14:18.130 --> 14:20.130
Usagimori Jizo  Mt. Rea Summit

14:20.130 --> 14:22.720
Fourth Runner: Hashimoto

14:25.280 --> 14:28.190
Fifth Runner: Albert

14:29.110 --> 14:30.280
Albert!

14:47.510 --> 14:49.660
Sixth Runner: Ishizaki

14:54.220 --> 14:56.170
Seventh Runner: Yukimura

15:02.150 --> 15:03.670
Yukimura!

15:07.520 --> 15:11.540
You made me run extra, so you'd 
better give this all you've got!

15:14.180 --> 15:15.080
I will!

15:33.290 --> 15:33.970
Sorry!

15:33.970 --> 15:34.970
We're still good.

15:54.490 --> 15:55.680
You did well.

15:56.440 --> 15:57.860
Leave the rest to me.

16:20.500 --> 16:21.750
Well, then...

16:22.390 --> 16:25.290
Perhaps I'll work up a bit of a sweat.

16:28.840 --> 16:31.890
You all did well over the eight 
days of this training camp.

16:33.240 --> 16:35.140
The average score was 
better than last year's.

16:35.970 --> 16:39.340
All of the boys' groups 
exceeded the borderline,

16:39.340 --> 16:41.400
so no one will be expelled.

16:42.990 --> 16:43.520
Hey.

16:44.570 --> 16:46.880
I always knew we'd get it done.

16:46.880 --> 16:48.280
Family.

16:48.280 --> 16:52.280
Incidentally, the highest overall 
score came from Class 3-A,

16:52.870 --> 16:54.600
Horikita Manabu's group.

16:54.600 --> 16:56.180
You did it, Horikita.

17:02.770 --> 17:06.050
Congratulations, Horikita-senpai.

17:06.050 --> 17:08.300
That's very impressive.

17:08.510 --> 17:11.050
It seems you lost, Nagumo.

17:11.430 --> 17:14.680
Well... that's up for debate.

17:16.180 --> 17:19.110
Meanwhile, in the girls' groups...

17:19.110 --> 17:23.020
I'm afraid there was one group 
that fell under the borderline.

17:23.920 --> 17:29.190
The group led by Ikari Momoko of Class 3-B.

17:37.170 --> 17:39.200
What the hell did you do, Nagumo?!

17:40.810 --> 17:43.990
Please calm down, Fujimaki-senpai.

17:44.330 --> 17:46.460
They're still announcing results.

17:47.240 --> 17:50.670
Why is Fujimaki-senpai of Class A so upset?

17:50.670 --> 17:53.280
The group leader was in Class B.

17:53.280 --> 17:56.220
The issue isn't the leader,

17:56.990 --> 17:59.100
but who she's taking with her.

17:59.950 --> 18:05.110
Unfortunately, Ikari will be expelled, 
along with a student she designates

18:05.110 --> 18:06.480
as sharing responsibility.

18:06.900 --> 18:09.390
Ikari, who do you designate?

18:09.390 --> 18:11.110
Who do you think?

18:11.760 --> 18:14.800
The one who disrupted the 
harmony of our group...

18:15.630 --> 18:17.740
Tachibana Akane-san!

18:18.620 --> 18:20.700
<i>It was all a trap by Nagumo.</i>

18:21.360 --> 18:24.020
<i>The duel was a distraction 
from his real objective.</i>

18:24.510 --> 18:27.630
<i>His target from the start 
was Tachibana Akane.</i>

18:28.750 --> 18:33.390
<i>Nagumo used girls loyal to 
his faction to create a group</i>

18:33.390 --> 18:37.280
<i>specifically designed to fall under 
the borderline and take Tachibana out.</i>

18:38.330 --> 18:41.740
Tachibana, why didn't you ask me for help?

18:42.140 --> 18:43.430
Because...

18:44.130 --> 18:48.130
I knew I would be a burden to you.

18:48.920 --> 18:50.190
I'm sorry.

18:50.190 --> 18:52.700
Friendship is a beautiful thing.

18:52.700 --> 18:55.450
Or should I call it "love"?

18:55.690 --> 18:59.450
Tell me <i>all</i> about how you feel right now.

19:00.010 --> 19:02.890
Are you more annoyed than 
you've ever been before?

19:03.570 --> 19:05.830
Why is Tachibana the one you targeted?

19:05.830 --> 19:12.590
I was just dying to see your 
face when I got rid of her.

19:12.590 --> 19:16.920
That indulgence of your curiosity 
has cost you something dear, Nagumo.

19:17.340 --> 19:21.630
Even if we did things differently, 
I still trusted you.

19:21.630 --> 19:25.100
And I'm choosing to throw 
that trust in your face.

19:25.100 --> 19:29.280
I'll expel as many people as I need to.

19:29.660 --> 19:33.360
That's how things are meant 
to be done at this school.

19:33.730 --> 19:35.850
<i>Nagumo's maliciousness won the day.</i>

19:36.430 --> 19:43.340
<i>But I doubt Horikita Manabu considered 
Tachibana an indispensable pawn.</i>

19:44.890 --> 19:50.250
You're talking as if Tachibana 
is going to be expelled.

19:51.560 --> 19:52.460
Sir.

19:53.890 --> 19:57.160
There's something I wish 
to spend points to buy.

19:57.160 --> 19:59.140
W-Wait, Horikita-kun!

19:59.140 --> 20:02.620
Wow, I thought we'd come out of this even.

20:02.620 --> 20:08.650
You're really going to spend all those 
points to save Tachibana-senpai?

20:08.910 --> 20:11.510
Please, don't! I've brought this on myself!

20:11.510 --> 20:13.270
Do you mind, everyone?

20:15.280 --> 20:17.090
Are you sure about this?

20:17.090 --> 20:20.280
You're effectively handing 
over your standing as Class A.

20:20.280 --> 20:24.950
Only until I take it back, though.

20:24.950 --> 20:26.410
Horikita-kun...

20:26.900 --> 20:30.170
Well, that's just fine by me.

20:31.280 --> 20:37.120
<i>I guess Nagumo isn't the 
only one with two faces.</i>

20:40.990 --> 20:42.940
It's absolutely unbelievable!

20:42.940 --> 20:45.930
I can't believe he cooked 
up a crazy plan like that.

20:45.930 --> 20:51.200
If I were that Ikari girl, 
I'd never volunteer to be expelled!

20:51.200 --> 20:54.260
Well, Ikari won't actually be expelled.

20:54.260 --> 20:55.940
How come?

20:55.940 --> 20:58.410
For the same reason as Tachibana Akane.

20:58.410 --> 21:01.970
She'll be saved from expulsion through the 
expenditure of large amounts of points.

21:02.570 --> 21:06.220
Nagumo would have agreed to cover that.

21:06.530 --> 21:09.710
Does that mean Nagumo-senpai 
lost a lot from this, too?

21:09.710 --> 21:12.880
The second-years are a monolith under Nagumo.

21:13.360 --> 21:16.130
They can easily afford it 
by pooling their resources.

21:16.710 --> 21:21.710
But Horikita Manabu has to pay 
with only one class's funds,

21:21.710 --> 21:23.390
so it's a more serious blow.

21:24.380 --> 21:26.720
It's such a reckless way to fight.

21:27.400 --> 21:31.850
That's how Nagumo Miyabi fights, I suppose.

21:31.850 --> 21:33.760
You didn't forget anything, did you?

21:33.760 --> 21:36.730
I said I checked. Just trust me!

21:37.230 --> 21:39.300
I guess we'd better split up.

21:39.730 --> 21:41.780
Wait, tell me one more thing!

21:43.560 --> 21:46.740
If I ended up in the same situation...

21:46.960 --> 21:48.750
What do you think you would—

21:48.750 --> 21:50.990
I wouldn't let you be expelled.

21:51.930 --> 21:54.000
I'd do whatever it takes.

21:59.700 --> 22:01.410
<i>What was to follow</i>

22:01.410 --> 22:07.220
<i>was a series of expulsions from 
Advanced Nurturing High School</i>

22:07.220 --> 22:09.330
<i>involving all class years.</i>
